BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Ironbark Repair Cafe) Tj T* () Tj T* (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY: IRONBARK REPAIR CAFE) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (When a household appliance or gadget stops working, most people throw it away and buy a new) Tj T* (one. Repair is often seen as inconvenient, uncertain or more expensive than replacement, and in) Tj T* (many neighborhoods there is simply no one nearby who will look at a broken toaster or a cracked) Tj T* (tablet. The result is a steady stream of electronic waste and a recurring cost that falls) Tj T* (hardest on lower-income households and renters, who can least afford to replace items that may) Tj T* (need only a small fix. Many of these failures are minor: a loose connection, a worn cord, a) Tj T* (dead battery, a blown fuse. Yet without access to tools, parts or knowledge, residents have few) Tj T* (options.) Tj T* () Tj T* (A second, related problem is everyday tech confusion. Many residents, particularly older) Tj T* (adults, struggle with slow computers, connectivity trouble and new devices, and they lack a) Tj T* (trusted, affordable place to ask for help in person.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Ironbark Repair Cafe is a walk-in neighborhood shop where residents bring broken electronics) Tj T* (and small appliances for low-cost repair and friendly tech troubleshooting. A customer walks) Tj T* (in, describes the problem, and a technician diagnoses the item at the counter whenever) Tj T* (possible. We then give a flat-rate quote before any work begins, so there are no surprises.) Tj T* (Simple repairs are completed while the customer waits or within a few days. Items that cannot) Tj T* (be fixed economically are recycled responsibly, and we tell the customer honestly when) Tj T* (replacement is the better choice.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We also offer short troubleshooting sessions, booked or walk-in, for problems such as slow) Tj T* (laptops, phone setup, printer trouble and Wi-Fi issues.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our approach is built on three ideas: transparent pricing, a welcoming space that does not) Tj T* (intimidate non-technical customers, and a focus on common items rather than specialized or) Tj T* (high-end equipment.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our target customers are residents of mixed-income urban neighborhoods, especially renters,) Tj T* (students, families on tight budgets and older adults. We believe these groups both generate) Tj T* (frequent small repair needs and are underserved by existing options. We estimate that an) Tj T* (average household owns dozens of small electronic devices and appliances and that a meaningful) Tj T* (share of these fail each year. Our initial plan is to serve a single neighborhood of roughly) Tj T* (twenty thousand residents near our university, with the goal of capturing a small percentage of) Tj T* (households as repeat customers within the first two years. We have not yet completed a formal) Tj T* (market study, and our sizing is based on public household statistics and informal conversations) Tj T* (with residents and property managers. If the first location performs well, we see room to) Tj T* (replicate the model in other neighborhoods and to add partnerships with landlords and housing) Tj T* (organizations.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Ironbark earns revenue in four ways. First, repair fees: flat-rate pricing by item category,) Tj T* (ranging from roughly ten dollars for simple fixes to around sixty dollars for more involved) Tj T* (work. Second, parts sales, with a modest markup on replacement components such as cords,) Tj T* (batteries and switches. Third, a small monthly membership, planned at around eight dollars,) Tj T* (that gives members discounted repairs and free basic troubleshooting. Fourth, business-to-) Tj T* (business contracts with landlords and property managers who need appliances maintained across) Tj T* (multiple units.) Tj T* () Tj ET
endstream
