BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Our main costs are rent, technician labor, parts inventory, tools and insurance. We expect a) Tj T* (typical month to require a minimum volume of repairs to cover fixed costs, and we are still) Tj T* (refining our estimate of that break-even point. Our current assumption is that a single) Tj T* (storefront can reach break-even at around eight to ten repairs per day, though this depends) Tj T* (heavily on local rent and our actual average ticket size.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (The space for repair is crowded and fragmented. Competitors include phone and computer repair) Tj T* (kiosks, which focus on a narrow set of high-volume devices; appliance repair services, which) Tj T* (typically target large appliances and charge house-call fees; big-box retailers that sell) Tj T* (replacements and offer limited service plans; and volunteer repair events that run occasionally) Tj T* (and cannot serve walk-in demand. Online tutorials also let some customers attempt their own) Tj T* (repairs.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We differentiate on convenience, price transparency and scope: we handle the small, everyday) Tj T* (items that others decline as not worth their time, in a neighborhood setting. We recognize that) Tj T* (this niche is not defended by any strong barrier. A competitor could copy our approach, and our) Tj T* (long-term advantage will depend on service quality, community trust and efficient operations) Tj T* (rather than proprietary technology.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marisol Tran-Whitfield, chief executive, is a senior studying business and has run a campus) Tj T* (electronics-swap event for two years. She leads operations and customer relationships. Devon) Tj T* (Okafor-Reyes, head of repairs, is an engineering student who has repaired consumer electronics) Tj T* (as a side business for several years and designed our diagnosis workflow. Priya Lindqvist, head) Tj T* (of finance and outreach, studies accounting and manages budgeting, pricing and partnerships) Tj T* (with local landlords and community groups. None of us has yet run a full-time retail business,) Tj T* (and we plan to seek advice from local shop owners and our university's entrepreneurship) Tj T* (mentors.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have defined our core concept and service menu, and we have built a working prototype of our) Tj T* (intake and diagnosis process, operated out of a borrowed workspace near our university. We have) Tj T* (formed a C corporation. Our first paying client, a local landlord, hired us to repair a batch) Tj T* (of tenant appliances, generating our first revenue. To date, revenue is small and has come from) Tj T* (this one customer and a few informal jobs for friends and classmates. We have not yet tracked) Tj T* (margins carefully.) Tj T* () Tj T* (For our first year, we project modest revenue growth as word spreads, assuming a storefront) Tj T* (opens within six months. Our early estimates suggest that a first location needs roughly forty) Tj T* (to fifty thousand dollars to cover build-out, tools, initial parts inventory, insurance and) Tj T* (several months of operating costs. We have no external funding at this time beyond founder) Tj T* (contributions, and we do not yet have a website.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to this competition for seed funding to help open our first storefront, as well) Tj T* (as mentorship on lease negotiation, pricing and retail operations. Prize funding would let us) Tj T* (secure space, purchase professional-grade tools and stock initial parts, moving us from a) Tj T* (borrowed workspace to a permanent presence in the neighborhood. We would also welcome) Tj T* (introductions to local property managers, community organizations and potential partners in) Tj T* (electronics recycling. With this support, we aim to open within six months, validate our break-) Tj T* (even assumptions with real data, and build a sustainable model that keeps useful products in) Tj T* (use and money in residents' pockets.) Tj ET
